PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L02U6.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":2,"cefr":"A1b","unit":6,"theme":"My Week","essential_question":"How do we balance work and fun in our week?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS1","title":"I Always Pray on Time: Adverbs of Frequency","objectives":["Students will be able to use always, usually, often, sometimes and never to say how often.","Students will be able to put adverbs of frequency before the main verb and after be.","I can say how often I do things.","I can put \"always\" and \"never\" in the right place."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام always وusually وoften وsometimes وnever للتعبير عن التكرار.","سيتمكن الطلاب من وضع ظرف التكرار قبل الفعل الأساسي وبعد فعل be.","أستطيع أن أقول كم مرة أفعل الأشياء.","أستطيع أن أضع always وnever في المكان الصحيح."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"always","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈɔlˌweɪz/","definition":"every time; 100%","arabic":"دائمًا","example":"I always say \"Bismillah\" before I eat.","image_id":"GV-L02-U6-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS1-W01"},{"word":"usually","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈjuʒəwəli/","definition":"almost every time; about 90%","arabic":"عادةً","example":"We usually eat lunch at two.","image_id":"GV-L02-U6-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS1-W02"},{"word":"often","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈɔfən/","definition":"many times","arabic":"غالبًا / كثيرًا","example":"My cousins often visit us.","image_id":"GV-L02-U6-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS1-W03"},{"word":"sometimes","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/səmˈtaɪmz/","definition":"not always, but some of the time","arabic":"أحيانًا","example":"It sometimes rains in March.","image_id":"GV-L02-U6-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Adverbs of frequency tell us how often something happens: always (100%), usually (90%), often (70%), sometimes (50%), never (0%).\nThey come before the main verb: He always prays on time. But they come after am/is/are: He is never late.\nnever is already negative – don't use it with don't: I never eat fast food (NOT I don't never eat).\nsubject + adverb + main verb: We usually walk.\nsubject + am/is/are + adverb: She is always happy.\nnever = 0% (no don't with never)\nsometimes can also start a sentence: Sometimes we eat out.","examples":["I always wash my hands before meals.","My mom usually drinks tea in the afternoon.","We often go to the park on Friday.","Yusuf sometimes helps his dad in the shop.","My little brother is never quiet!","They never eat dinner late.","It is usually hot in July.","Sometimes I read before bed."],"common_errors":["✗ I play always football. → ✓ I always play football. (The adverb goes before the main verb.)","✗ She always is happy. → ✓ She is always happy. (After is → the adverb.)","✗ I don't never eat candy. → ✓ I never eat candy. (never is already negative.)","✗ He never late. → ✓ He is never late. (Don't forget is.)"],"arabic":"ظروف التكرار: always (دائمًا) وusually (عادةً) وoften (غالبًا) وsometimes (أحيانًا) وnever (أبدًا).\nتأتي قبل الفعل الأساسي: I always pray، لكنها تأتي بعد am/is/are: He is always happy.\nnever منفية أصلًا، فلا نستخدم معها don't."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I Always Pray on Time: Adverbs of Frequency”. Let’s learn adverbs of frequency (always, usually, often, sometimes, never) and their position together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U6-LS1 | I Always Pray on Time: Adverbs of Frequency","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Faisal's Week”: Faisal is a busy boy. He always prays Fajr with his father. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Faisal is a busy boy. He always prays Fajr with his father.","visual":"Image GV-L02-U6-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Adverbs of frequency tell us how often something happens: always (100%), usually (90%), often (70%), sometimes (50%), never (0%). They come before the main verb: He always prays on time. But they come after am/is/are: He is never late.","on_screen":"subject + adverb + main verb: We usually walk. • subject + am/is/are + adverb: She is always happy. • never = 0% (no don't with never)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I always wash my hands before meals. My mom usually drinks tea in the afternoon. We often go to the park on Friday.","on_screen":"I always wash my hands before meals. / My mom usually drinks tea in the afternoon. / We often go to the park on Friday.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I play always football.” That’s not right. We say: “I always play football.” The adverb goes before the main verb.","on_screen":"✗ I play always football.   ✓ I always play football.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"He is never late.\" How many times is he late? … Think! … Zero times – never. Great job! Now you can say: I can say how often I do things.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say how often I do things.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: adverbs of frequency (always, usually, often, sometimes, never) and their position.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","ظروف التكرار: always (دائمًا) وusually (عادةً) وoften (غالبًا) وsometimes (أحيانًا) وnever (أبدًا).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I play always football. — الصحيح: I always play football.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول كم مرة أفعل الأشياء."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Faisal's Week","body":"Faisal is a busy boy. He always prays Fajr with his father.\nHe usually walks to school with his brother.\nOn Mondays and Wednesdays, he often goes to the swimming club.\nHe sometimes plays chess with his grandpa in the evening.\nHe is never late for school, and he never watches TV on school nights.\nOn the weekend, he usually visits his cousins, and they play football.\nFaisal loves his busy week!","word_count":72,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"I ___ brush my teeth at night. (100%)","options":["often","always","never","sometimes"],"answer":"always","explanation":"always 100% • usually 90% • often 70% • sometimes 50% • never 0%.","explanation_ar":"نسب التكرار."},{"q":"My dad ___ drinks soda. (0%)","options":["never","usually","always","often"],"answer":"never","explanation":"always 100% • usually 90% • often 70% • sometimes 50% • never 0%.","explanation_ar":"نسب التكرار."},{"q":"","options":["We eat usually lunch at two.","Usually we lunch eat at two.","We usually eat lunch at two.","We eat lunch usually at two."],"answer":"We usually eat lunch at two.","explanation":"Adverb of frequency goes before the main verb.","explanation_ar":"الظرف قبل الفعل الأساسي."},{"q":"","options":["She is always kind.","She always is kind.","She is kind always is.","Always she is kind."],"answer":"She is always kind.","explanation":"Adverb of frequency goes after am/is/are.","explanation_ar":"الظرف بعد am/is/are."},{"q":"","options":["I not never eat fast food.","I don't never eat fast food.","I never don't eat fast food.","I never eat fast food."],"answer":"I never eat fast food.","explanation":"never = 0%; don't use it with don't.","explanation_ar":"never منفية فلا نضع معها don't."},{"q":"It ___ snows in Riyadh. (almost 0%)","options":["usually","always","often","never"],"answer":"never","explanation":"always 100% • usually 90% • often 70% • sometimes 50% • never 0%.","explanation_ar":"نسب التكرار."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS1-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Put the adverb in the right place.","items":[{"q":"We go to the beach on Friday. (often)","options":[],"answer":"We often go to the beach on Friday.","explanation":"Adverb of frequency goes before the main verb.","explanation_ar":"الظرف قبل الفعل الأساسي."},{"q":"My grandma is busy. (always)","options":[],"answer":"My grandma is always busy.","explanation":"Adverb of frequency goes after am/is/are.","explanation_ar":"الظرف بعد am/is/are."},{"q":"I play video games. (sometimes)","options":[],"answer":"I sometimes play video games.","explanation":"Adverb of frequency goes before the main verb.","explanation_ar":"الظرف قبل الفعل الأساسي."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS1-B2","type":"order","instructions":"Guided practice: Put the words in order.","items":[{"q":"school / Fahad / usually / walks / to   ( . )","options":["school","Fahad","usually","walks","to"],"answer":"Fahad usually walks to school.","explanation":"Word order: Adverb of frequency goes before the main verb.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: الظرف قبل الفعل الأساسي."},{"q":"The / late / is / bus / never   ( . )","options":["The","late","is","bus","never"],"answer":"The bus is never late.","explanation":"Word order: Adverb of frequency goes after am/is/are.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: الظرف بعد am/is/are."},{"q":"eat / pizza / on / sometimes / Thursday / We   ( . )","options":["eat","pizza","on","sometimes","Thursday","We"],"answer":"We sometimes eat pizza on Thursday.","explanation":"Word order: Adverb of frequency goes before the main verb.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: الظرف قبل الفعل الأساسي."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write true sentences about you.","items":[{"q":"I always ___.","options":[],"answer":"I always help my mom.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of frequency (always, usually, often, sometimes, never) and their position correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I usually ___ after school.","options":[],"answer":"I usually do my homework after school.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of frequency (always, usually, often, sometimes, never) and their position correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I often ___ on the weekend.","options":[],"answer":"I often visit my cousins on the weekend.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of frequency (always, usually, often, sometimes, never) and their position correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I sometimes ___.","options":[],"answer":"I sometimes play chess.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of frequency (always, usually, often, sometimes, never) and their position correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I never ___.","options":[],"answer":"I never stay up after midnight.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of frequency (always, usually, often, sometimes, never) and their position correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Habit survey.","items":[{"q":"Ask 3 friends \"How often do you…?\" about one habit. Write their answers.","options":[],"answer":"Saad always eats breakfast. Ali sometimes eats breakfast. Fahad never eats breakfast.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of frequency (always, usually, often, sometimes, never) and their position correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 healthy habits and 1 unhealthy habit of your family with adverbs.","options":[],"answer":"We always drink water. My dad often walks. My brother sometimes eats too many sweets.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of frequency (always, usually, often, sometimes, never) and their position correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a \"never\" sentence about something you want to try.","options":[],"answer":"I never ride horses, but I want to try!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of frequency (always, usually, often, sometimes, never) and their position correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spin & Speak","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Work in teams of four. Player 1 spins the wheel.","Make a correct sentence about the unit theme using the cue word and adverbs of frequency (always, usually, often, sometimes, never) and their position.","The team checks the sentence with the grammar box. Correct = 1 point; an extra detail = 1 bonus point.","Pass the spinner clockwise. Play for 6 minutes; the team with most points wins."],"data":[{"label":"always"},{"label":"usually"},{"label":"often"},{"label":"sometimes"},{"label":"never"},{"label":"every day"},{"label":"once a week"},{"label":"twice a week"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"I ___ say \"Thank you\". (100%)","options":["never","always","sometimes","rarely"],"answer":"always","explanation":"always 100% • usually 90% • often 70% • sometimes 50% • never 0%.","explanation_ar":"نسب التكرار."},{"q":"","options":["My sister reads often stories.","My sister reads stories often reads.","My sister often reads stories.","Often my sister stories reads."],"answer":"My sister often reads stories.","explanation":"Adverb of frequency goes before the main verb.","explanation_ar":"الظرف قبل الفعل الأساسي."},{"q":"","options":["The shop is busy usually is.","Usually the shop busy is.","The shop usually is busy.","The shop is usually busy."],"answer":"The shop is usually busy.","explanation":"Adverb of frequency goes after am/is/are.","explanation_ar":"الظرف بعد am/is/are."},{"q":"","options":["We never don't go to bed late.","We don't never go to bed late.","We not never go to bed late.","We never go to bed late."],"answer":"We never go to bed late.","explanation":"never = 0%; don't use it with don't.","explanation_ar":"never منفية فلا نضع معها don't."},{"q":"My uncle ___ drives fast. He is careful.","options":["often","never","always","usually"],"answer":"never","explanation":"always 100% • usually 90% • often 70% • sometimes 50% • never 0%.","explanation_ar":"نسب التكرار."},{"q":"","options":["I help sometimes my dad wash the car.","Sometimes I help my dad sometimes wash the car.","I sometimes help my dad wash the car.","I help my dad sometimes wash the car."],"answer":"I sometimes help my dad wash the car.","explanation":"Adverb of frequency goes before the main verb.","explanation_ar":"الظرف قبل الفعل الأساسي."},{"q":"Which adverb means about 50%?","options":["sometimes","usually","never","always"],"answer":"sometimes","explanation":"always 100% • usually 90% • often 70% • sometimes 50% • never 0%.","explanation_ar":"نسب التكرار."},{"q":"","options":["They never are noisy in the library.","Never they are noisy in the library.","They are noisy never in the library.","They are never noisy in the library."],"answer":"They are never noisy in the library.","explanation":"Adverb of frequency goes after am/is/are.","explanation_ar":"الظرف بعد am/is/are."},{"q":"Grandpa ___ forgets his glasses. It happens a lot!","options":["often","doesn't","not","never"],"answer":"often","explanation":"always 100% • usually 90% • often 70% • sometimes 50% • never 0%.","explanation_ar":"نسب التكرار."},{"q":"","options":["Do you usually walk to school?","Do you walk usually to school?","Do usually you walk to school?","Usually do you walk to school?"],"answer":"Do you usually walk to school?","explanation":"Adverb of frequency goes before the main verb.","explanation_ar":"الظرف قبل الفعل الأساسي."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Faisal's weekly planner on a wall with pictures: praying with his father, walking to school, the swimming club, playing chess with Grandpa and playing football with cousins. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Faisal's weekly planner on a wall with pictures: praying with his father, walking to school, the swimming club, playing chess with Grandpa and playing football with cousins"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about adverbs of frequency (always, usually, often, sometimes, never) and their position, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about adverbs of frequency (always, usually, often, sometimes, never) and their position, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows always (every time; 100%); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing always: every time; 100%"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows usually (almost every time; about 90%); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing usually: almost every time; about 90%"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows often (many times); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing often: many times"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows sometimes (not always, but some of the time); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing sometimes: not always, but some of the time"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spin & Speak”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spin & Speak"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS1-W01","script":"always. always. I always say \"Bismillah\" before I eat.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS1-W02","script":"usually. usually. We usually eat lunch at two.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS1-W03","script":"often. often. My cousins often visit us.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS1-W04","script":"sometimes. sometimes. It sometimes rains in March.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS1-T1","script":"Faisal is a busy boy. He always prays Fajr with his father. He usually walks to school with his brother. On Mondays and Wednesdays, he often goes to the swimming club. He sometimes plays chess with his grandpa in the evening. He is never late for school, and he never watches TV on school nights. On the weekend, he usually visits his cousins, and they play football. Faisal loves his busy week!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I Always Pray on Time: Adverbs of Frequency”. Let’s learn adverbs of frequency (always, usually, often, sometimes, never) and their position together. Listen to the start of “Faisal's Week”: Faisal is a busy boy. He always prays Fajr with his father. Look at the green words. Adverbs of frequency tell us how often something happens: always (100%), usually (90%), often (70%), sometimes (50%), never (0%). They come before the main verb: He always prays on time. But they come after am/is/are: He is never late. Here are some examples. I always wash my hands before meals. My mom usually drinks tea in the afternoon. We often go to the park on Friday. Be careful! Some learners say: “I play always football.” That’s not right. We say: “I always play football.” The adverb goes before the main verb. Quick check: \"He is never late.\" How many times is he late? … Think! … Zero times – never. Great job! Now you can say: I can say how often I do things.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS2","title":"How Often? Once a Week, on Mondays, in May","objectives":["Students will be able to ask and answer How often…? with once, twice, every and on Mondays.","Students will be able to use on with dates and in with months and years.","I can ask \"How often do you play football?\" and answer \"Twice a week.\"","I can say \"on May 5\" and \"in 2026\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من السؤال والإجابة بـ How often…؟ باستخدام once وtwice وevery.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام on مع التواريخ وin مع الشهور والسنوات.","أستطيع أن أسأل How often do you play football? وأجيب Twice a week.","أستطيع أن أقول on May 5 وin 2026."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"never","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈnɛvɚ/","definition":"not at any time; 0%","arabic":"أبدًا","example":"My grandpa never drinks soda.","image_id":"GV-L02-U6-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS2-W01"},{"word":"hobby","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhɑbi/","definition":"something you enjoy doing in your free time","arabic":"هواية","example":"Drawing is my favorite hobby.","image_id":"GV-L02-U6-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS2-W02"},{"word":"weekend","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈwiˌkɛnd/","definition":"Friday and Saturday in Saudi Arabia; days with no school","arabic":"عطلة نهاية الأسبوع","example":"We go to the farm on the weekend.","image_id":"GV-L02-U6-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS2-W03"},{"word":"chess","pos":"noun","ipa":"/tʃɛs/","definition":"a game for two players on a board with 64 squares","arabic":"الشطرنج","example":"Grandpa teaches me chess.","image_id":"GV-L02-U6-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Ask How often…? to find out how many times: How often do you go swimming? – Twice a week.\nAnswers: once a week (1 time), twice a week (2 times), three times a month, every day, every Friday. On Mondays (with -s) means every Monday.\nPrepositions of time: on + day or date (on Monday, on May 5), in + month, season or year (in May, in winter, in 2026). In American English we say on the weekend.","examples":["How often do you do karate? – Once a week.","My brother goes to the gym three times a week.","We visit Grandma every Friday.","The science club meets on Wednesdays.","School starts in August.","My cousin was born in 2017.","The school trip is on March 12.","We go camping on the weekend."],"common_errors":["✗ How many times you play chess? → ✓ How often do you play chess? (Use How often do you…?)","✗ I play football two times in week. → ✓ I play football twice a week. (Say twice a week.)","✗ My birthday is in July 9. → ✓ My birthday is on July 9. (Dates → on.)","✗ She was born on 2016. → ✓ She was born in 2016. (Years → in.)"],"arabic":"نسأل How often…? (كم مرة؟) والإجابة: once a week (مرة في الأسبوع) وtwice a week (مرتين) وevery day (كل يوم).\non Mondays بالجمع تعني «كل يوم اثنين».\non مع التاريخ: on May 5، وin مع الشهر والسنة: in May وin 2026.\nفي الإنجليزية الأمريكية نقول on the weekend."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “How Often? Once a Week, on Mondays, in May”. Let’s learn How often…? with once / twice / three times a week, every…; prepositions of time with days, dates, months and years together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U6-LS2 | How Often? Once a Week, on Mondays, in May","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: I go swimming twice a week. • We have chess club on Tuesdays. • My birthday is on June 3. I don't go to the club every day. • We don't have school in August. How often do you visit your grandparents? – Every Friday. • When is the trip? – It's on May 5.","on_screen":"I go swimming twice a week. • We have chess club on Tuesdays. • My birthday is on June 3. | I don't go to the club every day. • We don't have school in August. | How often do you visit your grandparents? – Every Friday. • When is the trip? – It's on May 5.","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Ask How often…? to find out how many times: How often do you go swimming? – Twice a week. Answers: once a week (1 time), twice a week (2 times), three times a month, every day, every Friday. On Mondays (with -s) means every Monday.","on_screen":"How often…? with once / twice / three times a week, every…; prepositions of time with days, dates, months and years","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. How often do you do karate? – Once a week. My brother goes to the gym three times a week. We visit Grandma every Friday.","on_screen":"How often do you do karate? – Once a week. / My brother goes to the gym three times a week. / We visit Grandma every Friday.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “How many times you play chess?.” That’s not right. We say: “How often do you play chess?.” Use How often do you…?","on_screen":"✗ How many times you play chess?   ✓ How often do you play chess?","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"Twice a week\" – how many times? … Think! … Two times. Great job! Now you can say: I can ask \"How often do you play football?\" and answer \"Twice a week.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can ask \"How often do you play football?\" and answer \"Twice a week.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: How often…? with once / twice / three times a week, every…; prepositions of time with days, dates, months and years.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نسأل How often…? (كم مرة؟) والإجابة: once a week (مرة في الأسبوع) وtwice a week (مرتين) وevery day (كل يوم).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: How many times you play chess? — الصحيح: How often do you play chess?","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أسأل How often do you play football? وأجيب Twice a week."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"___ do you go to the library? – Once a week.","options":["When often","How much","How often","How many"],"answer":"How often","explanation":"Ask How often do/does…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ How often."},{"q":"I play tennis two times a week. = I play tennis ___ a week.","options":["every","twice","once","three times"],"answer":"twice","explanation":"once (1) • twice (2) • three times… + a week/a month; every + day/week.","explanation_ar":"once وtwice وthree times."},{"q":"My birthday is ___ April 20.","options":["on","at","by","in"],"answer":"on","explanation":"on + day or date.","explanation_ar":"on مع اليوم والتاريخ."},{"q":"We have exams ___ June.","options":["at","by","on","in"],"answer":"in","explanation":"in + month, season or year.","explanation_ar":"in مع الشهر والفصل والسنة."},{"q":"The chess club meets ___. (every Tuesday)","options":["on Tuesday's","in Tuesday","at Tuesdays","on Tuesdays"],"answer":"on Tuesdays","explanation":"On Mondays = every Monday.","explanation_ar":"On Mondays تعني كل يوم اثنين."},{"q":"My grandpa was born ___ 1960.","options":["on","at","in","by"],"answer":"in","explanation":"in + month, season or year.","explanation_ar":"in مع الشهر والفصل والسنة."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS2-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Answer with once, twice, three times or every.","items":[{"q":"Rakan swims: Monday and Thursday.  (How often?)","options":[],"answer":"Rakan swims twice a week.","explanation":"once (1) • twice (2) • three times… + a week/a month; every + day/week.","explanation_ar":"once وtwice وthree times."},{"q":"Noura draws: Sunday to Saturday.  (How often?)","options":[],"answer":"Noura draws every day.","explanation":"once (1) • twice (2) • three times… + a week/a month; every + day/week.","explanation_ar":"once وtwice وthree times."},{"q":"We eat at a restaurant: one time a month.  (How often?)","options":[],"answer":"We eat at a restaurant once a month.","explanation":"once (1) • twice (2) • three times… + a week/a month; every + day/week.","explanation_ar":"once وtwice وthree times."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS2-B2","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write on or in. Word bank: on, in","items":[{"q":"The new term starts ______ September.","options":[],"answer":"in","explanation":"in + month, season or year.","explanation_ar":"in مع الشهر والفصل والسنة."},{"q":"Our school trip is ______ February 14.","options":[],"answer":"on","explanation":"on + day or date.","explanation_ar":"on مع اليوم والتاريخ."},{"q":"It's very hot here ______ summer.","options":[],"answer":"in","explanation":"in + month, season or year.","explanation_ar":"in مع الشهر والفصل والسنة."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Answer about you.","items":[{"q":"How often do you visit your grandparents?","options":[],"answer":"I visit them every Friday.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses How often…? with once / twice / three times a week, every…; prepositions of time with days, dates, months and years correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How often do you play video games?","options":[],"answer":"I play once a week.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses How often…? with once / twice / three times a week, every…; prepositions of time with days, dates, months and years correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"When is your birthday?","options":[],"answer":"My birthday is on October 2.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses How often…? with once / twice / three times a week, every…; prepositions of time with days, dates, months and years correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What do you do on the weekend?","options":[],"answer":"I go to the park with my family.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses How often…? with once / twice / three times a week, every…; prepositions of time with days, dates, months and years correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How often do you read a book?","options":[],"answer":"I read a book twice a week.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses How often…? with once / twice / three times a week, every…; prepositions of time with days, dates, months and years correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: My activity calendar.","items":[{"q":"Make a weekly calendar with 3 activities and how often you do them.","options":[],"answer":"football – twice a week; chess – on Tuesdays; reading – every day","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses How often…? with once / twice / three times a week, every…; prepositions of time with days, dates, months and years correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences from your calendar.","options":[],"answer":"I play football twice a week. I play chess on Tuesdays. I read every day.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses How often…? with once / twice / three times a week, every…; prepositions of time with days, dates, months and years correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 important dates for your family with on.","options":[],"answer":"My brother's birthday is on May 9. Our holiday starts on June 20.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses How often…? with once / twice / three times a week, every…; prepositions of time with days, dates, months and years correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Tic-Tac-Grammar","mechanic":"tic_tac_toe","rules":["Two teams: X and O. Team X chooses a square.","Using the cue, the team says a correct sentence with How often…? with once / twice / three times a week, every…; prepositions of time with days, dates, months and years (the form in brackets: +, – or ?).","If the class and teacher agree it is correct, the team marks the square.","Three squares in a row wins. Play a second round with the grid turned around."],"data":[{"cue":"How often / you / play football / ?"},{"cue":"she / always / pray on time / +"},{"cue":"they / never / eat fast food / +"},{"cue":"How often / he / go swimming / ?"},{"cue":"I / sometimes / do karate / +"},{"cue":"we / usually / visit Grandma / on Friday"},{"cue":"How often / your dad / cook / ?"},{"cue":"Omar / often / play chess / +"},{"cue":"you / ever / be late / ?"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"___ does your dad go to work? – Every day.","options":["How many","How much","What often","How often"],"answer":"How often","explanation":"Ask How often do/does…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ How often."},{"q":"I visit the dentist two times a year. = I visit the dentist ___ a year.","options":["three","once","every","twice"],"answer":"twice","explanation":"once (1) • twice (2) • three times… + a week/a month; every + day/week.","explanation_ar":"once وtwice وthree times."},{"q":"The concert is ___ January 30.","options":["at","on","by","in"],"answer":"on","explanation":"on + day or date.","explanation_ar":"on مع اليوم والتاريخ."},{"q":"Eid is ___ spring this year.","options":["at","by","in","on"],"answer":"in","explanation":"in + month, season or year.","explanation_ar":"in مع الشهر والفصل والسنة."},{"q":"","options":["We go to the farm in weekend.","We go to the farm on the weekend.","We go to the farm at weekends on.","We go to the farm on weekend the."],"answer":"We go to the farm on the weekend.","explanation":"on + day or date.","explanation_ar":"on مع اليوم والتاريخ."},{"q":"","options":["My little sister was born in 2020.","My little sister was born on 2020.","My little sister was born in the 2020.","My little sister was born at 2020."],"answer":"My little sister was born in 2020.","explanation":"in + month, season or year.","explanation_ar":"in مع الشهر والفصل والسنة."},{"q":"","options":["How many times you go swimming?","How often do you go swimming?","How often you go swimming?","How often does you go swimming?"],"answer":"How often do you go swimming?","explanation":"Ask How often do/does…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ How often."},{"q":"Art club is ___. (every Thursday)","options":["at Thursdays","in Thursdays","on Thursdays","on Thursday's"],"answer":"on Thursdays","explanation":"On Mondays = every Monday.","explanation_ar":"On Mondays تعني كل يوم اثنين."},{"q":"","options":["I play chess once a week.","I play chess one time in week.","I play chess once week.","I play chess once in a week times."],"answer":"I play chess once a week.","explanation":"once (1) • twice (2) • three times… + a week/a month; every + day/week.","explanation_ar":"once وtwice وthree times."},{"q":"When is the school play? – ___","options":["It's on May 15.","It's May on 15.","It's at May 15.","It's in May 15."],"answer":"It's on May 15.","explanation":"on + day or date.","explanation_ar":"on مع اليوم والتاريخ."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A school activity calendar with club days circled: swimming twice a week, chess once a week, karate on Mondays, and a big trip marked on May 5. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A school activity calendar with club days circled: swimming twice a week, chess once a week, karate on Mondays, and a big trip marked on May 5"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of How often…? with once / twice / three times a week, every…; prepositions of time with days, dates, months and years: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “My Week”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of How often…? with once / twice / three times a week, every…"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows never (not at any time; 0%); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing never: not at any time; 0%"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows hobby (something you enjoy doing in your free time); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing hobby: something you enjoy doing in your free time"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows weekend (Friday and Saturday in Saudi Arabia; days with no school); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing weekend: Friday and Saturday in Saudi Arabia; days with no school"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows chess (a game for two players on a board with 64 squares); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing chess: a game for two players on a board with 64 squares"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Tic-Tac-Grammar”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Tic-Tac-Grammar"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS2-W01","script":"never. never. My grandpa never drinks soda.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS2-W02","script":"hobby. hobby. Drawing is my favorite hobby.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS2-W03","script":"weekend. weekend. We go to the farm on the weekend.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS2-W04","script":"chess. chess. Grandpa teaches me chess.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “How Often? Once a Week, on Mondays, in May”. Let’s learn How often…? with once / twice / three times a week, every…; prepositions of time with days, dates, months and years together. Remember these patterns: I go swimming twice a week. • We have chess club on Tuesdays. • My birthday is on June 3. I don't go to the club every day. • We don't have school in August. How often do you visit your grandparents? – Every Friday. • When is the trip? – It's on May 5. Ask How often…? to find out how many times: How often do you go swimming? – Twice a week. Answers: once a week (1 time), twice a week (2 times), three times a month, every day, every Friday. On Mondays (with -s) means every Monday. Here are some examples. How often do you do karate? – Once a week. My brother goes to the gym three times a week. We visit Grandma every Friday. Be careful! Some learners say: “How many times you play chess?.” That’s not right. We say: “How often do you play chess?.” Use How often do you…? Quick check: \"Twice a week\" – how many times? … Think! … Two times. Great job! Now you can say: I can ask \"How often do you play football?\" and answer \"Twice a week.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS3","title":"Play, Go, or Do? Hobbies and Activities","objectives":["Students will be able to use play, go and do with sports and hobbies correctly.","Students will be able to talk about their hobbies and free-time activities.","I can say \"play chess\", \"go swimming\" and \"do karate\".","I can talk about my hobbies."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام play وgo وdo مع الرياضات والهوايات بشكل صحيح.","سيتمكن الطلاب من التحدث عن هواياتهم وأنشطة وقت الفراغ.","أستطيع أن أقول play chess وgo swimming وdo karate.","أستطيع أن أتحدث عن هواياتي."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"karate","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kɚˈɑti/","definition":"a sport where you fight with hands and feet","arabic":"الكاراتيه","example":"Bandar does karate twice a week.","image_id":"GV-L02-U6-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS3-W01"},{"word":"drawing","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈdrɔɪŋ/","definition":"making pictures with a pencil or pen","arabic":"الرسم","example":"Her drawing of a falcon is amazing.","image_id":"GV-L02-U6-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS3-W02"},{"word":"swimming","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈswɪmɪŋ/","definition":"the sport of moving through water","arabic":"السباحة","example":"Swimming is good exercise.","image_id":"GV-L02-U6-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS3-W03"},{"word":"club","pos":"noun","ipa":"/klʌb/","definition":"a group of people who meet to do an activity","arabic":"نادٍ","example":"I joined the school science club.","image_id":"GV-L02-U6-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS3-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"English uses three verbs for activities. play + ball games and board games: play football, play chess. go + activities ending in -ing: go swimming, go camping, go shopping. do + other sports and activities: do karate, do yoga, do exercise.\nA hobby is something you enjoy in your free time: drawing, reading, collecting stamps, cooking.\nTalk about hobbies with like/love/enjoy + -ing: I love drawing. He enjoys reading.\nCollocations/phrases: play + football • basketball • tennis • chess • video games | go + swimming • cycling • camping • fishing • shopping | do + karate • exercise • yoga • gymnastics • homework","examples":["I play basketball after school.","We go camping in the desert in winter.","My cousin does karate on Mondays.","Drawing is my favorite hobby.","Grandpa loves playing chess.","The family goes fishing on the weekend.","My sister does gymnastics at the club.","Do you enjoy swimming?"],"common_errors":["✗ I play karate. → ✓ I do karate. (karate → do.)","✗ We go to swimming. → ✓ We go swimming. (No to before -ing activities.)","✗ He makes exercise every day. → ✓ He does exercise every day. (exercise → do.)","✗ I like draw. → ✓ I like drawing. (like + -ing for hobbies.)"],"arabic":"نستخدم play مع ألعاب الكرة وألعاب الطاولة: play football وplay chess.\nنستخدم go مع الأنشطة المنتهية بـ ing: go swimming (بدون to).\nنستخدم do مع رياضات أخرى مثل الكاراتيه: do karate وdo exercise."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Play, Go, or Do? Hobbies and Activities”. Let’s learn hobbies and activities; collocations with play, go and do together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U6-LS3 | Play, Go, or Do? Hobbies and Activities","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. karate: a sport where you fight with hands and feet. drawing: making pictures with a pencil or pen. swimming: the sport of moving through water.","on_screen":"karate | drawing | swimming","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"English uses three verbs for activities. play + ball games and board games: play football, play chess. go + activities ending in -ing: go swimming, go camping, go shopping. do + other sports and activities: do karate, do yoga, do exercise. A hobby is something you enjoy in your free time: drawing, reading, collecting stamps, cooking.","on_screen":"hobbies and activities; collocations with play, go and do","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I play basketball after school. We go camping in the desert in winter. My cousin does karate on Mondays.","on_screen":"I play basketball after school. / We go camping in the desert in winter. / My cousin does karate on Mondays.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I play karate.” That’s not right. We say: “I do karate.” karate → do.","on_screen":"✗ I play karate.   ✓ I do karate.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Which verb goes with \"camping\": play, go or do? … Think! … *go* camping. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"play chess\", \"go swimming\" and \"do karate\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"play chess\", \"go swimming\" and \"do karate\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: hobbies and activities; collocations with play, go and do.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم play مع ألعاب الكرة وألعاب الطاولة: play football وplay chess.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I play karate. — الصحيح: I do karate.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول play chess وgo swimming وdo karate."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct verb.","items":[{"q":"My brother ___ tennis on Saturday.","options":["plays","makes","goes","does"],"answer":"plays","explanation":"play + ball games and board games.","explanation_ar":"play مع ألعاب الكرة والطاولة."},{"q":"We ___ camping in the desert.","options":["go","do","play","make"],"answer":"go","explanation":"go + -ing activities (no to).","explanation_ar":"go مع أنشطة ing بدون to."},{"q":"Lina ___ yoga with her mom.","options":["plays","goes","makes","does"],"answer":"does","explanation":"do + karate, exercise, yoga, gymnastics.","explanation_ar":"do مع الكاراتيه والتمارين."},{"q":"Do you ___ video games?","options":["do","make","play","go"],"answer":"play","explanation":"play + ball games and board games.","explanation_ar":"play مع ألعاب الكرة والطاولة."},{"q":"My dad ___ fishing with his friends.","options":["makes","goes","does","plays"],"answer":"goes","explanation":"go + -ing activities (no to).","explanation_ar":"go مع أنشطة ing بدون to."},{"q":"I love ___ pictures of animals.","options":["draw","to drawing","draws","drawing"],"answer":"drawing","explanation":"like / love / enjoy + -ing.","explanation_ar":"بعد like وenjoy نستخدم ing."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the verb to the activities.","items":[{"q":"play","options":["football, chess, tennis","swimming, cycling, camping","pasta, soup, cakes","comics, stories, magazines","karate, exercise, gymnastics","stamps, coins, shells"],"answer":"football, chess, tennis","explanation":"play → football, chess, tennis. play + ball games and board games.","explanation_ar":"play مع ألعاب الكرة والطاولة."},{"q":"go","options":["football, chess, tennis","swimming, cycling, camping","pasta, soup, cakes","comics, stories, magazines","karate, exercise, gymnastics","stamps, coins, shells"],"answer":"swimming, cycling, camping","explanation":"go → swimming, cycling, camping. play + ball games and board games.","explanation_ar":"play مع ألعاب الكرة والطاولة."},{"q":"do","options":["football, chess, tennis","swimming, cycling, camping","pasta, soup, cakes","comics, stories, magazines","karate, exercise, gymnastics","stamps, coins, shells"],"answer":"karate, exercise, gymnastics","explanation":"do → karate, exercise, gymnastics. play + ball games and board games.","explanation_ar":"play مع ألعاب الكرة والطاولة."},{"q":"collect","options":["football, chess, tennis","swimming, cycling, camping","pasta, soup, cakes","comics, stories, magazines","karate, exercise, gymnastics","stamps, coins, shells"],"answer":"stamps, coins, shells","explanation":"collect → stamps, coins, shells. play + ball games and board games.","explanation_ar":"play مع ألعاب الكرة والطاولة."},{"q":"read","options":["football, chess, tennis","swimming, cycling, camping","pasta, soup, cakes","comics, stories, magazines","karate, exercise, gymnastics","stamps, coins, shells"],"answer":"comics, stories, magazines","explanation":"read → comics, stories, magazines. play + ball games and board games.","explanation_ar":"play مع ألعاب الكرة والطاولة."},{"q":"cook","options":["football, chess, tennis","swimming, cycling, camping","pasta, soup, cakes","comics, stories, magazines","karate, exercise, gymnastics","stamps, coins, shells"],"answer":"pasta, soup, cakes","explanation":"cook → pasta, soup, cakes. play + ball games and board games.","explanation_ar":"play مع ألعاب الكرة والطاولة."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about your free time.","items":[{"q":"My favorite hobby is ___.","options":[],"answer":"My favorite hobby is drawing.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses hobbies and activities; collocations with play, go and do correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I play ___ with my friends.","options":[],"answer":"I play football with my friends.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses hobbies and activities; collocations with play, go and do correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"On the weekend, I go ___.","options":[],"answer":"On the weekend, I go cycling.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses hobbies and activities; collocations with play, go and do correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I want to do ___ one day.","options":[],"answer":"I want to do karate one day.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses hobbies and activities; collocations with play, go and do correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I enjoy ___ because ___.","options":[],"answer":"I enjoy reading because the stories are exciting.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses hobbies and activities; collocations with play, go and do correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Club poster.","items":[{"q":"Design a club for your school. Write its name and 3 activities with play/go/do.","options":[],"answer":"Adventure Club: go camping, go hiking, play team games","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses hobbies and activities; collocations with play, go and do correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences inviting students to your club.","options":[],"answer":"Do you enjoy camping? Join our club! We go hiking every Thursday.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses hobbies and activities; collocations with play, go and do correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask a partner about his hobby. Write 2 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"Saad's hobby is chess. He plays chess with his grandpa.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses hobbies and activities; collocations with play, go and do correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Memory Match","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Place all cards face down in a grid.","Turn over two cards. If the word matches its definition, keep the pair and say a sentence with the word.","If not, turn them back over; the next player plays.","The player with the most pairs wins."],"data":[{"word":"always","match":"every time; 100%","arabic":"دائمًا"},{"word":"usually","match":"almost every time; about 90%","arabic":"عادةً"},{"word":"often","match":"many times","arabic":"غالبًا / كثيرًا"},{"word":"sometimes","match":"not always, but some of the time","arabic":"أحيانًا"},{"word":"never","match":"not at any time; 0%","arabic":"أبدًا"},{"word":"hobby","match":"something you enjoy doing in your free time","arabic":"هواية"},{"word":"weekend","match":"Friday and Saturday in Saudi Arabia; days with no school","arabic":"عطلة نهاية الأسبوع"},{"word":"chess","match":"a game for two players on a board with 64 squares","arabic":"الشطرنج"},{"word":"karate","match":"a sport where you fight with hands and feet","arabic":"الكاراتيه"},{"word":"drawing","match":"making pictures with a pencil or pen","arabic":"الرسم"},{"word":"swimming","match":"the sport of moving through water","arabic":"السباحة"},{"word":"club","match":"a group of people who meet to do an activity","arabic":"نادٍ"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"They ___ basketball in the gym.","options":["make","play","do","go"],"answer":"play","explanation":"play + ball games and board games.","explanation_ar":"play مع ألعاب الكرة والطاولة."},{"q":"We often ___ shopping on Thursday evening.","options":["do","go","play","make"],"answer":"go","explanation":"go + -ing activities (no to).","explanation_ar":"go مع أنشطة ing بدون to."},{"q":"My cousin ___ gymnastics.","options":["does","plays","goes","makes"],"answer":"does","explanation":"do + karate, exercise, yoga, gymnastics.","explanation_ar":"do مع الكاراتيه والتمارين."},{"q":"","options":["I do swimming twice a week to.","I go to swimming twice a week.","I play swimming twice a week.","I go swimming twice a week."],"answer":"I go swimming twice a week.","explanation":"go + -ing activities (no to).","explanation_ar":"go مع أنشطة ing بدون to."},{"q":"","options":["He plays karate at the club.","He does karate at the club.","He goes karate at the club.","He makes karate at the club."],"answer":"He does karate at the club.","explanation":"do + karate, exercise, yoga, gymnastics.","explanation_ar":"do مع الكاراتيه والتمارين."},{"q":"","options":["She enjoys cooking with her grandma.","She enjoy cooking with her grandma.","She enjoys to cooking with her grandma.","She enjoys cook with her grandma."],"answer":"She enjoys cooking with her grandma.","explanation":"like / love / enjoy + -ing.","explanation_ar":"بعد like وenjoy نستخدم ing."},{"q":"Which one goes with \"play\"?","options":["swimming","camping","chess","karate"],"answer":"chess","explanation":"play + ball games and board games.","explanation_ar":"play مع ألعاب الكرة والطاولة."},{"q":"Which one goes with \"go\"?","options":["tennis","chess","cycling","yoga"],"answer":"cycling","explanation":"go + -ing activities (no to).","explanation_ar":"go مع أنشطة ing بدون to."},{"q":"Which one goes with \"do\"?","options":["video games","fishing","football","exercise"],"answer":"exercise","explanation":"do + karate, exercise, yoga, gymnastics.","explanation_ar":"do مع الكاراتيه والتمارين."},{"q":"Something you enjoy in your free time is a ___.","options":["club","lesson","weekend","hobby"],"answer":"hobby","explanation":"like / love / enjoy + -ing.","explanation_ar":"بعد like وenjoy نستخدم ing."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"Three club rooms side by side: boys playing chess and football, children going swimming and cycling, and a karate class doing kicks. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Three club rooms side by side: boys playing chess and football, children going swimming and cycling, and a karate class doing kicks"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows karate (a sport where you fight with hands and feet); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing karate: a sport where you fight with hands and feet"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows drawing (making pictures with a pencil or pen); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing drawing: making pictures with a pencil or pen"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows swimming (the sport of moving through water); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing swimming: the sport of moving through water"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows club (a group of people who meet to do an activity); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing club: a group of people who meet to do an activity"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Memory Match”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Memory Match"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS3-W01","script":"karate. karate. Bandar does karate twice a week.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS3-W02","script":"drawing. drawing. Her drawing of a falcon is amazing.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS3-W03","script":"swimming. swimming. Swimming is good exercise.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS3-W04","script":"club. club. I joined the school science club.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Play, Go, or Do? Hobbies and Activities”. Let’s learn hobbies and activities; collocations with play, go and do together. Meet some new words. karate: a sport where you fight with hands and feet. drawing: making pictures with a pencil or pen. swimming: the sport of moving through water. English uses three verbs for activities. play + ball games and board games: play football, play chess. go + activities ending in -ing: go swimming, go camping, go shopping. do + other sports and activities: do karate, do yoga, do exercise. A hobby is something you enjoy in your free time: drawing, reading, collecting stamps, cooking. Here are some examples. I play basketball after school. We go camping in the desert in winter. My cousin does karate on Mondays. Be careful! Some learners say: “I play karate.” That’s not right. We say: “I do karate.” karate → do. Quick check: Which verb goes with \"camping\": play, go or do? … Think! … *go* camping. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"play chess\", \"go swimming\" and \"do karate\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS4","title":"On Friday, We Relax: Commas with Time Phrases and Dates","objectives":["Students will be able to put a comma after a time phrase at the start of a sentence.","Students will be able to write dates with commas (Friday, May 5, 2026).","I can write \"On Friday, we visit Grandma.\"","I can write a date like \"May 5, 2026\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من وضع فاصلة بعد عبارة الوقت في بداية الجملة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة التواريخ مع الفواصل.","أستطيع أن أكتب On Friday, we visit Grandma.","أستطيع أن أكتب تاريخًا مثل May 5, 2026."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"always","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈɔlˌweɪz/","definition":"every time; 100%","arabic":"دائمًا","example":"I always say \"Bismillah\" before I eat.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"usually","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈjuʒəwəli/","definition":"almost every time; about 90%","arabic":"عادةً","example":"We usually eat lunch at two.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"often","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈɔfən/","definition":"many times","arabic":"غالبًا / كثيرًا","example":"My cousins often visit us.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sometimes","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/səmˈtaɪmz/","definition":"not always, but some of the time","arabic":"أحيانًا","example":"It sometimes rains in March.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"never","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈnɛvɚ/","definition":"not at any time; 0%","arabic":"أبدًا","example":"My grandpa never drinks soda.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"hobby","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhɑbi/","definition":"something you enjoy doing in your free time","arabic":"هواية","example":"Drawing is my favorite hobby.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"When a sentence starts with a time phrase, put a comma after it: On Friday, we visit Grandma. In the morning, I pray Fajr. After school, I play chess.\nWhen the time phrase comes at the end, we don't need a comma: We visit Grandma on Friday.\nIn American dates, put a comma between the day and the year: May 5, 2026. With a weekday, add a comma after it too: Friday, May 5, 2026.\nTime phrase at the start → comma: On Mondays, I go swimming.\nTime phrase at the end → no comma: I go swimming on Mondays.\nDate: Month Day, Year → June 3, 2026\nWeekday, Month Day, Year → Sunday, June 3, 2026","examples":["On Thursday, we have art.","Every morning, my dad reads the Quran.","After lunch, I do my homework.","We go camping in winter.","The trip is on April 10, 2026.","On the weekend, we play football.","The party is on Saturday, June 6, 2026.","Twice a week, Lina goes to art club."],"common_errors":["✗ On Friday we visit Grandpa. → ✓ On Friday, we visit Grandpa. (Comma after the time phrase at the start.)","✗ I play chess, on Tuesdays. → ✓ I play chess on Tuesdays. (No comma when the time phrase is at the end.)","✗ May 5 2026 → ✓ May 5, 2026 (Comma between the day and the year.)","✗ On, Monday, I swim. → ✓ On Monday, I swim. (One comma, after the whole time phrase.)"],"arabic":"عندما تبدأ الجملة بعبارة زمنية نضع فاصلة بعدها: On Friday, we visit Grandma.\nإذا جاءت العبارة الزمنية في آخر الجملة فلا نضع فاصلة.\nفي التاريخ الأمريكي نضع فاصلة بين اليوم والسنة: May 5, 2026."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “On Friday, We Relax: Commas with Time Phrases and Dates”. Let’s learn commas after time phrases at the start of a sentence; commas in dates together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U6-LS4 | On Friday, We Relax: Commas with Time Phrases and Dates","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"When a sentence starts with a time phrase, put a comma after it: On Friday, we visit Grandma. In the morning, I pray Fajr. After school, I play chess.","on_screen":"commas after time phrases at the start of a sentence; commas in dates","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"When a sentence starts with a time phrase, put a comma after it: On Friday, we visit Grandma. In the morning, I pray Fajr. After school, I play chess. When the time phrase comes at the end, we don't need a comma: We visit Grandma on Friday.","on_screen":"Time phrase at the start → comma: On Mondays, I go swimming. • Time phrase at the end → no comma: I go swimming on Mondays. • Date: Month Day, Year → June 3, 2026","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. On Thursday, we have art. Every morning, my dad reads the Quran. After lunch, I do my homework.","on_screen":"On Thursday, we have art. / Every morning, my dad reads the Quran. / After lunch, I do my homework.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “On Friday we visit Grandpa.” That’s not right. We say: “On Friday, we visit Grandpa.” Comma after the time phrase at the start.","on_screen":"✗ On Friday we visit Grandpa.   ✓ On Friday, we visit Grandpa.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"After school I play.\" Where does the comma go? … Think! … After \"school\": After school, I play. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"On Friday, we visit Grandma.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"On Friday, we visit Grandma.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: commas after time phrases at the start of a sentence; commas in dates.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","عندما تبدأ الجملة بعبارة زمنية نضع فاصلة بعدها: On Friday, we visit Grandma.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: On Friday we visit Grandpa. — الصحيح: On Friday, we visit Grandpa.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب On Friday, we visit Grandma."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Noura's Diary (editing passage)","body":"Today is Thursday, March 5 2026. It was a busy day. In the morning I went to school. After lunch I did my art homework. I go to drawing club, on Thursdays. On the weekend we will visit my aunt.","word_count":40,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["On Sunday we have, a test.","On Sunday, we have a test.","On, Sunday we have a test.","On Sunday we, have a test."],"answer":"On Sunday, we have a test.","explanation":"Time phrase at the start → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية في البداية."},{"q":"","options":["I, read every night.","I read every, night.","I read, every night.","I read every night."],"answer":"I read every night.","explanation":"Time phrase at the end → no comma.","explanation_ar":"لا فاصلة إذا جاءت في النهاية."},{"q":"","options":["My birthday is on March 8, 2017.","My birthday is on March 8 2017.","My birthday is on, March 8 2017.","My birthday is on March, 8 2017."],"answer":"My birthday is on March 8, 2017.","explanation":"Comma between the day and the year (May 5, 2026).","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بين اليوم والسنة."},{"q":"","options":["In the evening, we drink tea.","In, the evening we drink tea.","In the evening we drink, tea.","In the, evening we drink tea."],"answer":"In the evening, we drink tea.","explanation":"Time phrase at the start → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية في البداية."},{"q":"","options":["The trip is on Tuesday May 12 2026.","The trip is on Tuesday, May 12 2026.","The trip is on Tuesday, May 12, 2026.","The trip is on, Tuesday May 12, 2026."],"answer":"The trip is on Tuesday, May 12, 2026.","explanation":"Comma after the weekday too (Friday, May 5, 2026).","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد اسم اليوم."},{"q":"","options":["We go, to the club twice a week.","We go to the club, twice a week.","We go to the club twice a week.","We go to the club twice, a week."],"answer":"We go to the club twice a week.","explanation":"Time phrase at the end → no comma.","explanation_ar":"لا فاصلة إذا جاءت في النهاية."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Add or remove a comma.","items":[{"q":"After school I do my homework.","options":[],"answer":"After school, I do my homework.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Time phrase at the start → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. فاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية في البداية."},{"q":"Every Friday we eat lunch with Grandpa.","options":[],"answer":"Every Friday, we eat lunch with Grandpa.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Time phrase at the start → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. فاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية في البداية."},{"q":"The match is on May 20 2026.","options":[],"answer":"The match is on May 20, 2026.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Comma between the day and the year (May 5, 2026).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. فاصلة بين اليوم والسنة."},{"q":"We visit the farm, on Saturdays.","options":[],"answer":"We visit the farm on Saturdays.","explanation":", → (delete). Time phrase at the end → no comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , → (delete). لا فاصلة إذا جاءت في النهاية."},{"q":"On the weekend my cousins come over.","options":[],"answer":"On the weekend, my cousins come over.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Time phrase at the start → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. فاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية في البداية."},{"q":"The museum opened on Monday June 1, 2026.","options":[],"answer":"The museum opened on Monday, June 1, 2026.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Comma after the weekday too (Friday, May 5, 2026).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. فاصلة بعد اسم اليوم."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit Noura's diary entry.","items":[{"q":"Today is Thursday, March 5 2026.","options":[],"answer":"Today is Thursday, March 5, 2026.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Time phrase at the start → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. فاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية في البداية."},{"q":"Today is Thursday, March 5 2026.","options":[],"answer":"Today is Thursday, March 5, 2026.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Time phrase at the start → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. فاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية في البداية."},{"q":"Today is Thursday, March 5 2026.","options":[],"answer":"Today is Thursday, March 5, 2026.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Time phrase at the start → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. فاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية في البداية."},{"q":"I go to drawing club, on Thursdays.","options":[],"answer":"I go to drawing club on Thursdays.","explanation":", → (delete). Time phrase at the start → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , → (delete). فاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية في البداية."},{"q":"Today is Thursday, March 5 2026.","options":[],"answer":"Today is Thursday, March 5, 2026.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Time phrase at the start → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. فاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية في البداية."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your week.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 sentences that start with a time phrase and a comma.","options":[],"answer":"On Monday, I go swimming. After school, I read. On the weekend, I visit my cousins.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commas after time phrases at the start of a sentence; commas in dates correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write today's date with the weekday.","options":[],"answer":"Tuesday, November 17, 2026","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commas after time phrases at the start of a sentence; commas in dates correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences with the time phrase at the end (no comma).","options":[],"answer":"I play chess on Wednesdays. We eat pizza on Thursday night.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commas after time phrases at the start of a sentence; commas in dates correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Builder","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["The teacher reads a word and a short clue.","Teams build the word with letter tiles in 30 seconds.","The team holds up the word; correct spelling = 1 point, with correct capital letter or punctuation where needed = 1 bonus point.","Continue until all words are used."],"data":[{"word":"always","clue":"every time; 100%"},{"word":"usually","clue":"almost every time; about 90%"},{"word":"sometimes","clue":"not always, but some of the time"},{"word":"weekend","clue":"Friday and Saturday in Saudi Arabia; days with no school"},{"word":"Wednesday","clue":""},{"word":"February","clue":""},{"word":"often","clue":"many times"},{"word":"never","clue":"not at any time; 0%"},{"word":"hobby","clue":"something you enjoy doing in your free time"},{"word":"chess","clue":"a game for two players on a board with 64 squares"},{"word":"karate","clue":"a sport where you fight with hands and feet"},{"word":"drawing","clue":"making pictures with a pencil or pen"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["On Mondays, I go to karate.","On Mondays I, go to karate.","On, Mondays I go to karate.","On Mondays I go, to karate."],"answer":"On Mondays, I go to karate.","explanation":"Time phrase at the start → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية في البداية."},{"q":"Where does the comma go? \"In winter we go camping.\"","options":["after \"In\"","after \"we\"","after \"winter\"","after \"go\""],"answer":"after \"winter\"","explanation":"Time phrase at the start → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية في البداية."},{"q":"","options":["Eid is on April, 9 2026.","Eid is on April 9, 2026.","Eid is on April 9 2026.","Eid is on, April 9 2026."],"answer":"Eid is on April 9, 2026.","explanation":"Comma between the day and the year (May 5, 2026).","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بين اليوم والسنة."},{"q":"","options":["I, usually sleep at ten.","I usually sleep at ten.","I usually, sleep at ten.","I usually sleep, at ten."],"answer":"I usually sleep at ten.","explanation":"Time phrase at the end → no comma.","explanation_ar":"لا فاصلة إذا جاءت في النهاية."},{"q":"","options":["Every morning Grandpa, walks in the park.","Every morning Grandpa walks, in the park.","Every, morning Grandpa walks in the park.","Every morning, Grandpa walks in the park."],"answer":"Every morning, Grandpa walks in the park.","explanation":"Time phrase at the start → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية في البداية."},{"q":"How many commas? \"Friday March 6 2026\"","options":["3","1","2","0"],"answer":"2","explanation":"Comma after the weekday too (Friday, May 5, 2026).","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد اسم اليوم."},{"q":"","options":["We have P.E. on, Tuesdays.","We have P.E., on Tuesdays.","We, have P.E. on Tuesdays.","We have P.E. on Tuesdays."],"answer":"We have P.E. on Tuesdays.","explanation":"Time phrase at the end → no comma.","explanation_ar":"لا فاصلة إذا جاءت في النهاية."},{"q":"","options":["After, dinner my dad tells us stories.","After dinner my dad tells us, stories.","After dinner my dad, tells us stories.","After dinner, my dad tells us stories."],"answer":"After dinner, my dad tells us stories.","explanation":"Time phrase at the start → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية في البداية."},{"q":"","options":["School finishes on Thursday, June 18, 2026.","School finishes on Thursday, June 18 2026.","School finishes on Thursday June, 18, 2026.","School finishes on Thursday June 18 2026."],"answer":"School finishes on Thursday, June 18, 2026.","explanation":"Comma after the weekday too (Friday, May 5, 2026).","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد اسم اليوم."},{"q":"Which sentence needs a comma?","options":["On Sunday we start a new lesson.","I swim every day.","We start a new lesson on Sunday.","We play on Friday."],"answer":"On Sunday we start a new lesson.","explanation":"Time phrase at the start → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية في البداية."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “My Week” that shows commas after time phrases at the start of a sentence; commas in dates in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “My Week” that shows commas after time phrases at the start of a sentence; commas in dates in action"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Builder”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Builder"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “On Friday, We Relax: Commas with Time Phrases and Dates”. Let’s learn commas after time phrases at the start of a sentence; commas in dates together. When a sentence starts with a time phrase, put a comma after it: On Friday, we visit Grandma. In the morning, I pray Fajr. After school, I play chess. When a sentence starts with a time phrase, put a comma after it: On Friday, we visit Grandma. In the morning, I pray Fajr. After school, I play chess. When the time phrase comes at the end, we don't need a comma: We visit Grandma on Friday. Here are some examples. On Thursday, we have art. Every morning, my dad reads the Quran. After lunch, I do my homework. Be careful! Some learners say: “On Friday we visit Grandpa.” That’s not right. We say: “On Friday, we visit Grandpa.” Comma after the time phrase at the start. Quick check: \"After school I play.\" Where does the comma go? … Think! … After \"school\": After school, I play. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"On Friday, we visit Grandma.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS5","title":"My Busy Week: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to interview a partner about his weekly activities.","Students will be able to write about their week with adverbs of frequency, hobbies and correct commas.","I can interview my partner about his week.","I can write a paragraph about my week."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من إجراء مقابلة مع زميل عن أنشطته الأسبوعية.","سيتمكن الطلاب من الكتابة عن أسبوعهم مع ظروف التكرار والهوايات والفواصل الصحيحة.","أستطيع أن أجري مقابلة مع زميلي عن أسبوعه.","أستطيع أن أكتب فقرة عن أسبوعي."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"always","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈɔlˌweɪz/","definition":"every time; 100%","arabic":"دائمًا","example":"I always say \"Bismillah\" before I eat.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"usually","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈjuʒəwəli/","definition":"almost every time; about 90%","arabic":"عادةً","example":"We usually eat lunch at two.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"often","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈɔfən/","definition":"many times","arabic":"غالبًا / كثيرًا","example":"My cousins often visit us.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sometimes","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/səmˈtaɪmz/","definition":"not always, but some of the time","arabic":"أحيانًا","example":"It sometimes rains in March.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"never","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈnɛvɚ/","definition":"not at any time; 0%","arabic":"أبدًا","example":"My grandpa never drinks soda.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"hobby","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhɑbi/","definition":"something you enjoy doing in your free time","arabic":"هواية","example":"Drawing is my favorite hobby.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"weekend","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈwiˌkɛnd/","definition":"Friday and Saturday in Saudi Arabia; days with no school","arabic":"عطلة نهاية الأسبوع","example":"We go to the farm on the weekend.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"chess","pos":"noun","ipa":"/tʃɛs/","definition":"a game for two players on a board with 64 squares","arabic":"الشطرنج","example":"Grandpa teaches me chess.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"karate","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kɚˈɑti/","definition":"a sport where you fight with hands and feet","arabic":"الكاراتيه","example":"Bandar does karate twice a week.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"drawing","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈdrɔɪŋ/","definition":"making pictures with a pencil or pen","arabic":"الرسم","example":"Her drawing of a falcon is amazing.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"swimming","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈswɪmɪŋ/","definition":"the sport of moving through water","arabic":"السباحة","example":"Swimming is good exercise.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"club","pos":"noun","ipa":"/klʌb/","definition":"a group of people who meet to do an activity","arabic":"نادٍ","example":"I joined the school science club.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 6: adverbs of frequency, How often…?, once/twice/every, on/in with days, dates and months, play/go/do and commas with time phrases and dates.\nA good \"My Week\" paragraph tells what you do, how often you do it and when.\n✔ adverb before the main verb / after be\n✔ once a week, twice a week, every day, on Mondays\n✔ play / go / do + activity\n✔ comma after a time phrase at the start","examples":["I usually play chess on Tuesday.","On Fridays, we always eat lunch at Grandpa's house.","My brother goes swimming twice a week.","How often do you do exercise? – Every day.","My sister is never bored.","In summer, we often go camping in Abha.","Majed sometimes does gymnastics.","The book fair is on May 3, 2026."],"common_errors":["✗ I go always to the club. → ✓ I always go to the club. (Adverb before the main verb.)","✗ I play karate on Mondays. → ✓ I do karate on Mondays. (karate → do.)","✗ On Tuesday I play football. → ✓ On Tuesday, I play football. (Comma after the time phrase at the start.)"],"arabic":"نراجع ظروف التكرار وHow often وplay/go/do وحروف الوقت والفواصل.\nالفقرة الجيدة عن أسبوعك تقول ماذا تفعل وكم مرة ومتى.\nتذكّر: الظرف قبل الفعل، وفاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية في بداية الجملة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “My Busy Week: Language in Use”. Let’s learn adverbs of frequency, How often, play/go/do, time prepositions and commas (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U6-LS5 | My Busy Week: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: \"Find someone who…\" survey: find classmates who always eat breakfast, never play video games, go swimming once a week, do karate, and play chess on the weekend. Write their names and one detail.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 6: adverbs of frequency, How often…?, once/twice/every, on/in with days, dates and months, play/go/do and commas with time phrases and dates. A good \"My Week\" paragraph tells what you do, how often you do it and when.","on_screen":"✔ adverb before the main verb / after be • ✔ once a week, twice a week, every day, on Mondays • ✔ play / go / do + activity","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I usually play chess on Tuesday. On Fridays, we always eat lunch at Grandpa's house. My brother goes swimming twice a week.","on_screen":"I usually play chess on Tuesday. / On Fridays, we always eat lunch at Grandpa's house. / My brother goes swimming twice a week.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I go always to the club.” That’s not right. We say: “I always go to the club.” Adverb before the main verb.","on_screen":"✗ I go always to the club.   ✓ I always go to the club.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “I play karate on Mondays.”? … Think! … It should be “I do karate on Mondays.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can interview my partner about his week.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can interview my partner about his week.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: adverbs of frequency, How often, play/go/do, time prepositions and commas (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع ظروف التكرار وHow often وplay/go/do وحروف الوقت والفواصل.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I go always to the club. — الصحيح: I always go to the club.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أجري مقابلة مع زميلي عن أسبوعه."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"My Busy Week – Adam","body":"I always go to school from Sunday to Thursday.\nOn Mondays and Wednesdays, I do karate at the sports club.\nI usually play basketball with my cousins on Tuesday.\nI sometimes go cycling in the park, but I never ride on the busy road.\nOn the weekend, my family often visits my grandparents.\nMy week is busy, but I love it!","word_count":61,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Adam's text. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Adam goes to school from Sunday to Thursday.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Busy Week – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"He does karate on Tuesdays.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “My Busy Week – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"He usually plays basketball with his cousins.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Busy Week – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"He often rides his bike on the busy road.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “My Busy Week – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"His family often visits his grandparents on the weekend.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Busy Week – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Adam doesn't like his busy week.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “My Busy Week – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"","options":["Adam goes cycling sometimes goes.","Adam sometimes goes cycling.","Adam goes sometimes cycling.","Sometimes Adam cycling goes."],"answer":"Adam sometimes goes cycling.","explanation":"Adverb before the main verb / after am, is, are.","explanation_ar":"مكان ظرف التكرار."},{"q":"___ does Adam do karate? – Twice a week.","options":["What often","How much","How often","How many"],"answer":"How often","explanation":"How often + do/does…? once / twice / every.","explanation_ar":"How often وإجاباتها."},{"q":"Adam ___ karate at the sports club.","options":["plays","does","makes","goes"],"answer":"does","explanation":"play (games) / go (-ing) / do (karate, exercise).","explanation_ar":"play وgo وdo."},{"q":"The book fair is ___ May 3.","options":["on","at","by","in"],"answer":"on","explanation":"on + day/date; in + month/year.","explanation_ar":"on للأيام والتواريخ وin للشهور والسنوات."},{"q":"","options":["On, the weekend we visit our grandparents.","On the weekend we visit, our grandparents.","On the weekend we, visit our grandparents.","On the weekend, we visit our grandparents."],"answer":"On the weekend, we visit our grandparents.","explanation":"Comma after a time phrase at the start.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية."},{"q":"My little brother is ___ quiet. He talks all the time!","options":["never","often","usually","always"],"answer":"never","explanation":"Adverb before the main verb / after am, is, are.","explanation_ar":"مكان ظرف التكرار."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Find someone who… Write names and details.","items":[{"q":"Find someone who always eats breakfast.","options":[],"answer":"Saad always eats eggs for breakfast.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of frequency, How often, play/go/do, time prepositions and commas (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Find someone who never plays video games.","options":[],"answer":"Fahad never plays video games. He reads instead.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of frequency, How often, play/go/do, time prepositions and commas (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Find someone who goes swimming once a week.","options":[],"answer":"Ali goes swimming every Monday.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of frequency, How often, play/go/do, time prepositions and commas (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Find someone who does karate.","options":[],"answer":"Turki does karate twice a week.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of frequency, How often, play/go/do, time prepositions and commas (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Find someone who plays chess on the weekend.","options":[],"answer":"Ziyad plays chess with his uncle on Friday.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of frequency, How often, play/go/do, time prepositions and commas (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write \"My Busy Week\".","items":[{"q":"Plan: list your activities and how often you do them.","options":[],"answer":"football – twice a week; reading – every day; swimming – on Saturdays","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of frequency, How often, play/go/do, time prepositions and commas (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 6 sentences with adverbs, play/go/do and commas.","options":[],"answer":"I always pray on time. On Mondays, I play football. I go swimming twice a week. I usually read before bed. On the weekend, I visit my grandparents. I never stay up late.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of frequency, How often, play/go/do, time prepositions and commas (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: adverb position? play/go/do? commas? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"I play karate\" to \"I do karate\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of frequency, How often, play/go/do, time prepositions and commas (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Quiz Show Challenge","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Teams take turns choosing a category and a cue word.","Grammar: make a sentence with adverbs of frequency, How often, play/go/do, time prepositions and commas (unit review). Words: give the meaning. Spelling: spell it. Write It!: write a sentence with correct punctuation.","Correct answers score 10 points; teams may steal a question another team misses.","The highest score after 8 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"always","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"usually","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"often","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"sometimes","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"never","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"hobby","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"weekend","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"chess","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"karate","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"drawing","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"swimming","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"club","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["My dad drives us usually to school drives.","Usually my dad us drives to school.","My dad drives usually us to school.","My dad usually drives us to school."],"answer":"My dad usually drives us to school.","explanation":"Adverb before the main verb / after am, is, are.","explanation_ar":"مكان ظرف التكرار."},{"q":"","options":["How often do you do your homework?","How often does you do your homework?","How often you do your homework?","How many do you do your homework?"],"answer":"How often do you do your homework?","explanation":"How often + do/does…? once / twice / every.","explanation_ar":"How often وإجاباتها."},{"q":"Do you ___ fishing with your uncle?","options":["go","play","make","do"],"answer":"go","explanation":"play (games) / go (-ing) / do (karate, exercise).","explanation_ar":"play وgo وdo."},{"q":"The new term starts ___ January.","options":["on","at","in","by"],"answer":"in","explanation":"on + day/date; in + month/year.","explanation_ar":"on للأيام والتواريخ وin للشهور والسنوات."},{"q":"Where does the comma go? \"On Thursday evening we go out.\"","options":["after \"On\"","after \"go\"","after \"evening\"","after \"we\""],"answer":"after \"evening\"","explanation":"Comma after a time phrase at the start.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية."},{"q":"","options":["My cousins play volleyball every Friday.","My cousins go volleyball every Friday.","My cousins play volleyball every Fridays.","My cousins do volleyball every Friday."],"answer":"My cousins play volleyball every Friday.","explanation":"play (games) / go (-ing) / do (karate, exercise).","explanation_ar":"play وgo وdo."},{"q":"","options":["Always the baby hungry is!","The baby is hungry always is!","The baby always is hungry!","The baby is always hungry!"],"answer":"The baby is always hungry!","explanation":"Adverb before the main verb / after am, is, are.","explanation_ar":"مكان ظرف التكرار."},{"q":"I do yoga three times a ___.","options":["weeks","weekend","week","weekly"],"answer":"week","explanation":"How often + do/does…? once / twice / every.","explanation_ar":"How often وإجاباتها."},{"q":"","options":["Saudi National Day is at September 23.","Saudi National Day is on September 23.","Saudi National Day is in September 23.","Saudi National Day is September on 23."],"answer":"Saudi National Day is on September 23.","explanation":"on + day/date; in + month/year.","explanation_ar":"on للأيام والتواريخ وin للشهور والسنوات."},{"q":"Choose the best sentence for \"My Week\":","options":["On, Sundays I usually go to library.","On Sundays, I usually go to the library.","On Sundays I go usually to the library.","On Sundays, I usually go to the library on."],"answer":"On Sundays, I usually go to the library.","explanation":"Comma after a time phrase at the start.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Omar and Adam sitting with a weekly planner, comparing their activities with colored stickers for sports, clubs and family time. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Omar and Adam sitting with a weekly planner, comparing their activities with colored stickers for sports, clubs and family time"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “My Week”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “My Week”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L02-U6-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Quiz Show Challenge”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Quiz Show Challenge"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS5-T1","script":"I always go to school from Sunday to Thursday. On Mondays and Wednesdays, I do karate at the sports club. I usually play basketball with my cousins on Tuesday. I sometimes go cycling in the park, but I never ride on the busy road. On the weekend, my family often visits my grandparents. My week is busy, but I love it!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U6-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “My Busy Week: Language in Use”. Let’s learn adverbs of frequency, How often, play/go/do, time prepositions and commas (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: \"Find someone who…\" survey: find classmates who always eat breakfast, never play video games, go swimming once a week, do karate, and play chess on the weekend. Write their names and one detail. Today you use all of Unit 6: adverbs of frequency, How often…?, once/twice/every, on/in with days, dates and months, play/go/do and commas with time phrases and dates. A good \"My Week\" paragraph tells what you do, how often you do it and when. Here are some examples. I usually play chess on Tuesday. On Fridays, we always eat lunch at Grandpa's house. My brother goes swimming twice a week. Be careful! Some learners say: “I go always to the club.” That’s not right. We say: “I always go to the club.” Adverb before the main verb. Quick check: what is wrong with “I play karate on Mondays.”? … Think! … It should be “I do karate on Mondays.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can interview my partner about his week.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"I ___ wash my hands before meals. (100%)","options":["sometimes","often","always","never"],"answer":"always","explanation":"always 100% • usually 90% • often 70% • sometimes 50% • never 0%.","explanation_ar":"نسب التكرار."},{"q":"","options":["Often we football play after school.","We often play football after school.","We play often football after school.","We play football often after school play."],"answer":"We often play football after school.","explanation":"Adverb of frequency goes before the main verb.","explanation_ar":"الظرف قبل الفعل الأساسي."},{"q":"","options":["The teacher is on time always is.","The teacher always is on time.","The teacher is always on time.","Always the teacher is on time."],"answer":"The teacher is always on time.","explanation":"Adverb of frequency goes after am/is/are.","explanation_ar":"الظرف بعد am/is/are."},{"q":"","options":["I never don't drink cold water in winter.","I don't never drink cold water in winter.","I never drink cold water in winter.","I not never drink cold water in winter."],"answer":"I never drink cold water in winter.","explanation":"never = 0%; don't use it with don't.","explanation_ar":"never منفية فلا نضع معها don't."},{"q":"Which adverb means 0%?","options":["often","never","usually","sometimes"],"answer":"never","explanation":"always 100% • usually 90% • often 70% • sometimes 50% • never 0%.","explanation_ar":"نسب التكرار."},{"q":"___ do you visit the dentist? – Twice a year.","options":["How much","How many","When often","How often"],"answer":"How often","explanation":"Ask How often do/does…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ How often."},{"q":"She reads the newspaper every day. = She reads it ___.","options":["daily","once a week","twice a month","never"],"answer":"daily","explanation":"once (1) • twice (2) • three times… + a week/a month; every + day/week.","explanation_ar":"once وtwice وthree times."},{"q":"My brother's wedding is ___ June 12.","options":["on","by","in","at"],"answer":"on","explanation":"on + day or date.","explanation_ar":"on مع اليوم والتاريخ."},{"q":"My grandpa came to Taif ___ 1985.","options":["at","on","by","in"],"answer":"in","explanation":"in + month, season or year.","explanation_ar":"in مع الشهر والفصل والسنة."},{"q":"The drawing club meets ___. (every Sunday)","options":["on Sunday's","on Sundays","in Sunday","at Sundays"],"answer":"on Sundays","explanation":"On Mondays = every Monday.","explanation_ar":"On Mondays تعني كل يوم اثنين."},{"q":"My cousins ___ volleyball at the beach.","options":["go","do","play","make"],"answer":"play","explanation":"play + ball games and board games.","explanation_ar":"play مع ألعاب الكرة والطاولة."},{"q":"We ___ hiking in the mountains.","options":["do","go","make","play"],"answer":"go","explanation":"go + -ing activities (no to).","explanation_ar":"go مع أنشطة ing بدون to."},{"q":"My sister ___ gymnastics at the club.","options":["goes","plays","makes","does"],"answer":"does","explanation":"do + karate, exercise, yoga, gymnastics.","explanation_ar":"do مع الكاراتيه والتمارين."},{"q":"","options":["I enjoy collecting stamps.","I enjoy to collecting stamps.","I enjoys collecting stamps.","I enjoy collect stamps."],"answer":"I enjoy collecting stamps.","explanation":"like / love / enjoy + -ing.","explanation_ar":"بعد like وenjoy نستخدم ing."},{"q":"Something you do for fun in your free time is a ___.","options":["lesson","test","hobby","job"],"answer":"hobby","explanation":"like / love / enjoy + -ing.","explanation_ar":"بعد like وenjoy نستخدم ing."},{"q":"Pick the activity we use with \"do\".","options":["karate","chess","basketball","fishing"],"answer":"karate","explanation":"do + karate, exercise, yoga, gymnastics.","explanation_ar":"do مع الكاراتيه والتمارين."},{"q":"","options":["On, Tuesdays we have science club.","On Tuesdays, we have science club.","On Tuesdays we have, science club.","On Tuesdays we, have science club."],"answer":"On Tuesdays, we have science club.","explanation":"Time phrase at the start → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية في البداية."},{"q":"","options":["I have swimming lessons on Mondays.","I have swimming, lessons on Mondays.","I have swimming lessons, on Mondays.","I, have swimming lessons on Mondays."],"answer":"I have swimming lessons on Mondays.","explanation":"Time phrase at the end → no comma.","explanation_ar":"لا فاصلة إذا جاءت في النهاية."},{"q":"","options":["Our school opened on September 1 2015.","Our school opened on, September 1 2015.","Our school opened on September, 1 2015.","Our school opened on September 1, 2015."],"answer":"Our school opened on September 1, 2015.","explanation":"Comma between the day and the year (May 5, 2026).","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بين اليوم والسنة."},{"q":"","options":["The exam is on, Monday May 18, 2026.","The exam is on Monday, May 18, 2026.","The exam is on Monday May 18 2026.","The exam is on Monday, May 18 2026."],"answer":"The exam is on Monday, May 18, 2026.","explanation":"Comma after the weekday too (Friday, May 5, 2026).","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد اسم اليوم."},{"q":"Where does the comma go? \"After Maghrib we eat dinner.\"","options":["after \"eat\"","after \"we\"","after \"After\"","after \"Maghrib\""],"answer":"after \"Maghrib\"","explanation":"Time phrase at the start → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد العبارة الزمنية في البداية."},{"q":"Choose the best sentence for a weekly plan:","options":["On Wednesdays, I usually go karate.","On, Wednesdays I usually play karate.","On Wednesdays I do usually karate.","On Wednesdays, I usually do karate."],"answer":"On Wednesdays, I usually do karate.","explanation":"play (games) / go (-ing) / do (karate, exercise).","explanation_ar":"play وgo وdo."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"i play always chess on fridays.\"","options":["i always play chess on fridays.","I play always chess on Fridays.","I always play chess on Fridays.","I always play chess on fridays."],"answer":"I always play chess on Fridays.","explanation":"Adverb of frequency goes before the main verb.","explanation_ar":"الظرف قبل الفعل الأساسي."},{"q":"How often do you go to the mosque? – ___","options":["Five times a day.","Five times in day.","Five day a times.","In five times a day."],"answer":"Five times a day.","explanation":"once (1) • twice (2) • three times… + a week/a month; every + day/week.","explanation_ar":"once وtwice وthree times."}],"theme_ar":"أسبوعي","essential_question_ar":"كيف نوازن بين العمل والمرح في أسبوعنا؟","can_do":"I can say how often I do things and talk about my hobbies and my weekly timetable.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أقول كم مرة أفعل الأشياء، وأتحدث عن هواياتي وجدولي الأسبوعي."});
